#!/bin/bash
#MISE description="Boot each shipped level with NO env vars and fail on any panic"
# Every other check here runs with VOXEL_REMOTE, VOXEL_START and friends
# set, so a system that only fails on a PLAIN launch survives all of them.
# That is exactly what happened: `HostCommands` is created by the remote
# plugin, and requiring it panicked the whole schedule on every ordinary
# `cargo run` while every test passed.
#
# Usage: mise run smoke [seconds]
set -e
SECS=${1:-25}
cargo build -p voxel2 2>&1 | tail -1
status=0
for level in levels/*.json; do
    log=$(mktemp)
    caffeinate -dis ./target/debug/voxel2 "$level" > "$log" 2>&1 &
    pid=$!
    sleep "$SECS"
    kill "$pid" 2>/dev/null || true
    wait "$pid" 2>/dev/null || true
    for bad in "panicked" "error in system" "Validation Error" "never became drawable"; do
        n=$(grep -c "$bad" "$log" || true)
        if [ "$n" != "0" ]; then
            echo "FAIL $level: $n x '$bad'"
            grep -m2 "$bad" "$log"
            status=1
        fi
    done
    [ "$status" = "0" ] && echo "ok   $level"
    rm -f "$log"
done
[ "$status" = "0" ] && echo "SMOKE PASS" || echo "SMOKE FAIL"
exit $status
